Patch G3, shim as a module (rung 2, task T0b): g3-crate-batch-3.patch for
the owner's O3 answer "a module inside eng-platform-winit". Apply it after
g2-crates.patch and g2-gcmouse-module.patch, instead of
g3-crate-batch-3.patch. That file's header gives the batch, its two
differences from the plan's list, the notes on bincode-next's licence,
typos and MSRVs, and how the batch was resolved; all hold here.

The only differences from g3-crate-batch-3.patch:
- the wrapper ban names eng-platform-winit:
  `{ crate = "objc2-game-controller", wrappers = ["eng-platform-winit"] }`,
  with its comment saying why;
- the batch 3 comment calls the shim a module of eng-platform-winit.
The same 17 names, with `objc2-game-controller:*`.

Base: main at c879061 with g2-crates.patch and g2-gcmouse-module.patch
applied. At the repo root, run `git apply` with this file, then
`cargo xtask quick` and `cargo xtask ci --job lint`.
Text before the first `diff --git` line is ignored by `git apply`.

How it was tested, on aarch64-apple-darwin with Rust 1.99.1, cargo-deny
0.20.2 and typos-cli 1.51.1, in scratch clones of c879061 with those two
patches applied:
- `git apply --check` and `git apply` give the tested files byte for byte;
  `cargo xtask quick` and `CI=1 cargo xtask ci --job lint` are 7 of 7.
- In a scratch copy (not part of this patch), gungraun =0.20.0 in
  eng-bench's Linux dev-dependencies and objc2-game-controller =0.3.2 (the
  shim's features) in eng-platform-winit's macOS dependencies:
  `cargo deny check` exits 0, all four checks ok, no warning beyond
  today's. objc2-game-controller in eng-app as well: bans fails with
  `error[banned]`.

diff --git a/deny.toml b/deny.toml
index 0f1a64be48db4379cd4603ed0008fb1f258447b4..6ce3e3749fa9e2474414af116c4863c5ede082b7 100644
--- a/deny.toml
+++ b/deny.toml
@@ -62,6 +62,10 @@ deny = [
     "wgpu", "wgpu-core", "wgpu-hal", "wgpu-types", "winit",
     "eng-platform-api", "eng-platform-winit", "eng-gpu", "eng-app",
   ] },
+  # The Game Controller bindings stay inside eng-platform-winit, whose GCMouse
+  # shim module is the one place that calls them with `unsafe` (rung 2,
+  # decision 11, O3).
+  { crate = "objc2-game-controller", wrappers = ["eng-platform-winit"] },
   # Unmaintained (spec 6.8).
   { crate = "laminar" },
   { crate = "bincode" },
@@ -80,6 +84,11 @@ deny = [
 # every target above. wgpu, winit and raw-window-handle are also in `deny`
 # with their wrappers, and cargo-deny refuses the same spec in both lists, so
 # here they are written `name:*` (any release version).
+# Batch 3, approved by the owner at gate G3 for rung 2 ("Crate batch 3" in
